(2,9,5), m = 10 = 2w instance), so "a lift with u_lift > 2w —
realizable" is false there; and at even N the sentence "different
deep lifts realize different residual classes, hence different σ"
is unjustified in char 2 (dμ < w forces the S₁-slot to 0 and
T² + S₀ is always a square over F_{q²}: the read is REFINE, not a
decided σ). The corrected per-stratum witnesses (2w ≥ N throughout;
u-geography from GENH4-7'(a): u_lift sweeps {N, N+1, …} at a
band-zero state and {N, …, m} at a band-pinned state; legs per
GENH4-3 + GENH4-CAP(F): u odd ≤ 2w → RAM(u), σ = {(2,2)}; u even
= 2dμ ≤ 2w → residual read at depth dμ; u > 2w → 2SIDED,
σ = {(1,2),(1,2)}):

* **N odd (both strata, both characteristics).** Lift 1: u = N (odd,
  ≤ 2w) → RAM(N) → {(2,2)}. Lift 2, by stratum: band-zero, or
  band-pinned with m > 2w: u > 2w resp. u = m > 2w → 2SIDED →
  {(1,2),(1,2)} ≠ {(2,2)}. Band-pinned with m ≤ 2w (the Codex
  instance): take u = N+1 (even, ≤ m ≤ 2w): residual read at
  dμ₁ = (N+1)/2 with the free a₀ lift digit at height N+1 as its
  S₀-slot; if dμ₁ < w the S₁-slot is 0 and char ≠ 2 gives a DECIDED
  read for any nonzero digit ('11' → {(1,2),(1,2)} or '2' →
  {(1,4)}, either ≠ {(2,2)}), while char 2 gives '1sq' → carry ONE
  refine step (below); if dμ₁ = w (N+1 = 2w) the S₁-slot is the pin
  letter ≠ 0, the residual is separable in both characteristics,
  and any nonzero digit gives a decided '11'/'2' ≠ {(2,2)}. At
  Codex's (2,9,5): RAM(9) = {(2,2)} vs the u = 10, dμ₁ = 5 = w
  separable read — witnesses exist; the old display's u > 2w lift
  indeed does not.
* **N even, dμ := N/2 < w (⟺ 2w ≥ N+2 — covers Codex's
  (q,k,N,w) = (2,1,6,4)).** Lift 1: u = N+1 (odd, ≤ 2w since
  2w ≥ N+2) → RAM(N+1) → {(2,2)} — realizable in every stratum (at
  a band-pinned state with m = N+1 the height-(N+1) letter has
  d₁ ≠ 0, forcing u = N+1 for any a₀ digit; else the free a₀ digit
  at N+1 pins it). Lift 2: band-zero or m > 2w: u > 2w → 2SIDED →
  {(1,2),(1,2)}; band-pinned with m ≤ 2w: u = N residual read at
  depth dμ < w (S₁-slot 0): char ≠ 2 decided ≠ {(2,2)} as above;
  char 2: '1sq' → one refine step. NO residual-class comparison is
  needed in this sub-case — the char-2 even-N gap of the old
  display is bypassed by the RAM(N+1) leg.
* **N even, dμ = w (2w = N exactly).** Here every lift has u = 2w
  (the S₁ ≠ 0 separable residual read) or u > 2w (2SIDED,
  {(1,2),(1,2)}); no odd leg exists. The differing pair needs an
  INERT ('2') continuation at u = 2w, and its existence is a
  member-existence statement over the leaf key: the S₀-slot sweeps
  the F_q-line c·F_q (c = the fixed height-N normalizer twist unit
  of S3; the height-N letter has its a₁-component leaf-pinned to
  zero, so only the a₀ lift digit d₀ ∈ F_q moves), and:
  **char 2:** inert ⟺ Tr_{F_{q²}/F₂}(S₀/S₁²) = 1
  = Tr_{F_q/F₂}(d₀ · τ) with τ := Tr_{F_{q²}/F_q}(c/S₁²); since
  squaring is the Frobenius bijection of F_{q²}, S₁²  sweeps
  F_{q²}^× as the pin letter S₁ sweeps it, so c/S₁² sweeps
  F_{q²}^×, and Tr_{F_{q²}/F_q} is not identically zero there:
