## 5. Slice conclusion

No surviving argument in this slice is intrinsically mixed-characteristic-only: the actual counting and transport mechanisms use finite residue-field censuses, Newton-polygon/residual-polynomial combinatorics, quotient-ring digit bijections, and completeness/Hensel lifting. Equal-characteristic inseparability is a real issue, but the notes ultimately handle it correctly by restricting splitting-type assertions to `disc ≠ 0`; the one false unrestricted formulation is explicitly withdrawn. Thus the cubic and quartic mechanisms appear to need no new equal-characteristic mathematics. Two qualifications prevent an unconditional “GENERAL” certification: the published scope of the load-bearing Ore/GMN citation is not documented, and GENIND’s all-degree result remains conditional on open composite-stage work, now including the per-genre `(CS-1Q)` ledger. The latter is an incompleteness of the general induction, not a `F_q[[t]]` obstruction.

